& [Expectation] is a reviewed predicted disposition for one named stage and case
& [Observation] is the immutable result emitted by an actual admitted stage
& [Agreement] is a comparison conclusion licensed by one CommonSyntaxClaim after both observations match their expectations
  + observation equality alone is insufficient

& [CommonSyntaxClaim] is a proposition both selected readers are designed to observe
& [SchemaWitness] maps the claim to schema rule classes and normalized schema locations
& [TypedWitness] maps the claim to actual serde binding behavior and typed destinations
  + witness mappings may use different rule vocabularies

& [AcceptedAgreement] means both applicable readers ran accepted and were expected to accept the same claim
& [RejectedAgreement] means both applicable readers ran rejected as expected and each rejection maps to the same claim
& [ReaderDisagreement] means applicable readers have opposite accepted or rejected dispositions
& [ReasonMismatch] means both rejected but their mapped rejection claims differ or are unproven
& [ExpectationMismatch] means any observation differs from its own reviewed expectation
& [NotComparable] means no common claim licenses comparison
& [BlockedComparison] means ingress prerequisite dependency exhaustion or internal fault prevents a comparison conclusion

& [SemanticExpectation] is never part of syntax agreement
  + safe pure semantic execution has its own expected and actual dispositions
  + semantic agreement with expectation does not authorize use

& [CoverageClosure] means every mandatory obligation has at least one explicit satisfied edge and no contradictory edge
& [ResidualClosure] means every applicable residual has cases or an explicit non-passing deferred record
& [FinitePass] means zero findings both closures exact resource accounts and byte-identical replay for the admitted finite corpus
  + finite pass is not exhaustive equivalence

& [ReportCore] is the canonical deterministic projection of one complete pure evaluation
& [ReplayEnvelope] is the canonical comparison record for two independently recomputed cores
& [RefinedDisposition] is exact_inactive_i03e_formation
